// THE SECOND TRIVIALITY ROUTE: the conditions contain a proposition and its own NEGATION, so
// the antecedent is unsatisfiable by propositional logic alone.
//
// This is `swap`'s two trivial pairs (std/set/finite.b4m), and it is a DIFFERENT mechanism
// from a constructor split: it rests on NO axioms, where the constructor route needs the
// sort's disequality via its vacuity schema. Hence no `(theory)` selector here — there is no
// schema to find.
//
// `tautology` cannot discharge this: it sees `x = u` and `not (x = u)` as unrelated atoms and
// declines with a countermodel. The certificate walks the (nested) conjunction with
// `and_lhs`/`and_rhs` and finishes with `ex_falso`.
sort E

intheory complementaryPair

theorem complementaryPair: forall x, u, v: E; (x = u and (x != u and x != v)) -> v = x
proof
  @conclusion |
    forall x, u, v: E; (x = u and (x != u and x != v)) -> v = x
    [using definition_consistency]
qed
